/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:11:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:12:Move the orange rectangle onto the maroon rectangle and mark gated corridor crossings in red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:13:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:14:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:15:- The dominant background contains black obstacle segments.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:16:- There is one solid orange rectangle and one solid maroon rectangle of the same size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:17:- The two rectangles share either their row span or their column span, so the move is straight and axis-aligned.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:18:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:19:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:20:- Erase the original orange rectangle to the background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:21:- Replace the maroon rectangle with the orange rectangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:22:- Between the two rectangles, paint red across the moving rectangle's width or height only at corridor cells flanked by black obstacle segments perpendicular to the movement.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:23:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:24:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:25:- The black segments define gates in the straight corridor; only those gated openings, not every swept background cell, become red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:26:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:27:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:28:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:29:<reference_puzzle index="2" source="train" puzzle_id="396d80d7" lines="18-30">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:30:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:31:Paint the inner foreground color into every background pixel that touches the enclosing frame only diagonally.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:32:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:33:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:34:- The grid has one dominant background color and exactly two foreground colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:35:- One foreground color is an enclosing frame: its bbox strictly contains the bbox of the other, inner color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:36:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:37:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:38:- Keep all existing pixels unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:39:- For each background pixel, if it is diagonally adjacent to the frame color and has no orthogonal adjacency to the frame color, recolor it to the inner color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:40:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:41:Key insight: The inner color marks the color to use, while the frame's diagonal-only background neighbors define the cells to add.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:42:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:43:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:44:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:45:<reference_puzzle index="3" source="train" puzzle_id="22806e14" lines="23-37">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:46:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:47:Mark the center of each odd-sized solid square with the plus marker color, erasing the marker only when it is outside the marked-center field.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:48:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:49:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:50:- The dominant color is background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:51:- Exactly two foreground colors are present: one unique 3x3 plus marker and one color forming separated solid square objects.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:52:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:53:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:54:- For every non-marker 4-connected object, assert it is a solid square.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:55:- If the square side length is odd, recolor its center pixel to the plus marker color; even-sided squares stay unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:56:- Preserve the plus marker when its center lies inside the bounding box of the odd-square centers; otherwise erase it to background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:57:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:58:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:59:- Odd-sided solid squares have a single visible center pixel, and the plus supplies the color used to identify those centers.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:60:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:61:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:62:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:63:<reference_puzzle index="4" source="train" puzzle_id="5a719d11" lines="44-59">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:64:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:65:Within each horizontal pair of two-color panels, swap the motif masks and recolor each pasted mask with the source panel's base color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:66:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:67:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:68:- A separator color forms full blank rows and at least one full blank column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:69:- The non-separator area is split into row bands, each containing exactly two same-shaped rectangular panels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:70:- Each panel has a dominant base color and one minority motif color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:71:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:72:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:73:- For every row band, clear each panel to its own base color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:74:- Paste the right panel's motif mask into the left panel using the right base color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:75:- Paste the left panel's motif mask into the right panel using the left base color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:76:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:77:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:78:- The motif colors themselves are distractors; only each motif's shape mask and the two panel base colors are exchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:79:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:80:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:81:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:82:<reference_puzzle index="5" source="train" puzzle_id="13f06aa5" lines="36-51">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:83:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:84:Extend each colored marker from its directional sprite to a grid edge, painting a dotted ray and the whole edge side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:85:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:86:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:87:- The background is the dominant color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:88:- One repeated body color forms small 8-connected directional sprites.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:89:- Each marker is a singleton non-background, non-body color embedded in one sprite.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:90:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:91:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:92:- The body pixels around a marker lie mostly behind it; the opposite direction is the marker's ray direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:93:- Paint every second pixel from the marker along that ray, then paint the entire boundary side reached by the ray.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:94:- If two painted boundary sides meet at a corner, make that shared corner black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:95:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:96:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:97:- The same seven-pixel body sprite rotates to encode the direction; its local center-of-mass bias points away from the ray.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:98:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:99:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:100:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:101:<reference_puzzle index="6" source="eval" puzzle_id="31f7f899" lines="7-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:102:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:103:Sort vertical bars by height and redistribute them across fixed colored slots.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:104:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:105:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:106:- bg background; a horizontal base line of a single color spans the full grid width.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:107:- Several monochrome vertical bars of distinct colors rise upward from the base line.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:108:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:109:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:110:- Rank bar shapes by height (shortest to tallest).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:111:- Rank original x-positions (slots) left to right.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:112:- Place the i-th shortest shape into the i-th leftmost slot, recoloring it to that slot's original color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:113:- The base line is preserved unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:114:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:115:Key insight: Each slot keeps its x-position and color identity; only the bar silhouettes are redistributed among slots by height order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:116:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:117:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:118:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:119:<reference_puzzle index="7" source="train" puzzle_id="97c75046" lines="88-107">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:120:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:121:Move the single marker to the endpoint reached by sliding along the obstacle contour.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:122:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:123:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:124:- A dominant background color fills the canvas.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:125:- One single-pixel marker sits away from a connected obstacle region of the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:126:  remaining color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:127:- The marker has exactly one horizontal or vertical sightline to the obstacle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:128:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:129:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:130:- Find the last background pixel before the obstacle along that sightline.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:131:- From that pixel, try the two diagonal turns that continue around the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:132:  obstacle boundary.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:133:- Move the marker to the endpoint of the turn that remains 4-adjacent to the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:134:  obstacle for the longest distance.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:135:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:136:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:137:The marker is not placed by distance to the obstacle; it first points to the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:138:obstacle, then follows the visible outside contour until that contour segment ends.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:139:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:140:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:141:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:142:<reference_puzzle index="8" source="train" puzzle_id="b74ca5d1" lines="157-172">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:143:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:144:Swap each 5x5 sprite with its corner marker color and stamp same-marker composite masks into the matching corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:145:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:146:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:147:- A 30x30 grid has one dominant background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:148:- Non-background corner pixels are marker labels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:149:- Every other foreground color is the body of one 5x5 sprite containing exactly one pixel of a corner marker color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:150:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:151:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:152:- For each sprite, recolor body pixels to the sprite marker color and recolor the marker pixel back to its body color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:153:- If a marker lies on the side facing its matching corner and another same-marker sprite has a body pixel at that same local cell, use that visible body color for the marker pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:154:- For each corner marker, overlay the masks of all sprites with that marker color into the corner 5x5 block and paint the visible composite with the marker color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:155:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:156:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:157:The corner pixels are labels that group 5x5 sprites by their embedded marker color; each labeled corner shows the grouped sprite silhouette.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:158:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:159:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:160:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:161:<reference_puzzle index="9" source="eval" puzzle_id="dd6b8c4b" lines="9-22">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:162:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:163:Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:164:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:165:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:166:- bg = orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon (9) pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:167:- A unique red (2) pixel marks the center of a 3×3 destination block.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:168:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:169:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:170:- Maroon pixels connected to the destination through floor/maroon cells (not blocked by walls) are candidates.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:171:- Rank candidates by distance to the destination; the closest ones fill the block in row-major order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:172:- Moved maroons are erased (replaced with floor color).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:173:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:174:Key insight: Wall barriers restrict connectivity — only maroon pixels reachable via flood-fill through the floor qualify, so proximity alone isn't enough.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:175:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:176:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:177:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:178:<reference_puzzle index="10" source="train" puzzle_id="7d7772cc" lines="70-92">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:179:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:180:Move each source pixel toward the separator when it matches its aligned reference pixel, otherwise to the far edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:181:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:182:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:183:- A single full separator line is part of a rectangular frame; the frame's
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:184:  extra cells mark the reference side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:185:- On the reference side, one row or column of colored pixels is aligned
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:186:  with one row or column of source pixels on the opposite side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:187:- Each side has its own dominant background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:188:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:189:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:190:- Compare each source pixel with the reference pixel on the same row or column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:191:- If their colors match, place the source pixel in the cell adjacent to the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:192:  separator on the source side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:193:- If their colors differ, place the source pixel on the far outer edge along
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:194:  the same row or column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:195:- Erase the original source pixels to the source-side background; keep the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:196:  frame and reference pixels unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:197:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:198:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:199:The extra frame cells identify which side is the reference; equality with the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:200:aligned reference pixel decides whether each source pixel moves inward or outward.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:201:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:202:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:203:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:204:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="train" puzzle_id="52364a65" lines="10-24">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:205:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:206:Erase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:207:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:208:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:209:- A grid has one dominant background color and several monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:210:- Each foreground object spans at least two columns in its bounding box.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:211:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:212:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:213:- Find each same-color 4-connected foreground object.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:214:- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:215:- Leave all other pixels unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:216:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:217:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:218:- The deletion is measured from each object's local left edge, not from the grid edge or from a shared global column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:219:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:220:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:221:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:222:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="train" puzzle_id="c920a713" lines="87-102">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:223:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:224:Untangle overlapping colored rectangular frames into concentric square frames ordered by their visible crossings.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:225:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:226:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:227:- The background contains several one-cell-thick axis-aligned rectangular frames, one color per frame.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:228:- Frames overlap, and the visible color at an overlap records a directed crossing from the hidden frame to the visible frame.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:229:- Each foreground color still has visible pixels on the perimeter of its full rectangular bounding box.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:230:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:231:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:232:- Infer each color's full rectangular frame from the bounding box of its visible pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:233:- Add a directed edge A -> B when B is visible at a crossing of A and B's frame perimeters.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:234:- Find the unique path that visits every frame color once, then render those colors as one-pixel-thick concentric square frames from outside to inside.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:235:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:236:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:237:- The output is not a crop of the input; the crossing graph gives a single frame order, and that order is redrawn as nested rings.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:238:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:239:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:240:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:241:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="train" puzzle_id="e3fe1151" lines="36-55">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:242:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:243:Fill the one blank in each corner region so all four regions have the same color multiset.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:244:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:245:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:246:- The dominant background color forms one solid separator row and one solid
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:247:  separator column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:248:- The separator cross splits the grid into four equal rectangular corner regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:249:- Each corner region contains exactly one background-colored blank pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:250:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:251:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:252:- Count the non-background colors in each corner region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:253:- The completed region multiset is defined by the maximum observed count of
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:254:  each color across the four regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:255:- Replace each region's blank pixel with the single color needed to match that
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:256:  completed multiset.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:257:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:258:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:259:- The separator color inside a corner region is a missing value marker; comparing
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:260:  the four regions reveals the shared multiset without using numeric color order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:261:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:262:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:263:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:264:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="eval" puzzle_id="8b9c3697" lines="9-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:265:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:266:Insert red components into interior sockets of large structures, leaving a black trail.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:267:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:268:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:269:- bg = most common. Large non-bg, non-red structures with interior cavities.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:270:- Red components outside structures.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:271:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:272:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:273:- Interior sockets: bg cells inside a structure's bbox, adjacent to structure pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:274:- For each structure, find the direction where rays from sockets hit a red component.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:275:- Slide that component into the socket; paint traversed cells black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:276:- Unmatched reds vanish.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:277:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:278:Key insight: Docking direction is inferred by ray-casting from interior sockets to the nearest red component.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:279:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:280:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:281:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:282:<reference_puzzle index="15" source="train" puzzle_id="8dab14c2" lines="120-133">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:283:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:284:Complete each boundary tab or notch by adding the complementary feature on the opposite side of the foreground object.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:285:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:286:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:287:- The grid has exactly two colors: a dominant background and one foreground object.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:288:- The foreground object is a thick rectilinear shape with one-pixel tabs and notches on its boundary.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:289:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:290:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:291:- A foreground tab is a one-neighbor boundary pixel; project through its full row or column span and remove the opposite edge pixel to make a matching notch.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:292:- A background notch is a one-pixel cut with three foreground 4-neighbors; project across the full row or column span and add a tab just outside the opposite edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:293:- Notches immediately beside a tab source are not independent sources, because that gap belongs to the tab's local boundary shape.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:294:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:295:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:296:- The changed pixels are not color-specific noise; they are paired jigsaw-like boundary features on opposite sides of the same thick row or column cross-section.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:297:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:298:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:299:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:300:<reference_puzzle index="16" source="train" puzzle_id="e39e9282" lines="73-81">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:301:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:302:Project maroon markers into adjacent grey or pink 3x3 squares, erasing grey squares afterward.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:303:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:304:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:305:The grid has a dominant background, solid 3x3 grey and/or pink squares, and maroon marker pixels or segments directly touching one side of exactly one square.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:306:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:307:Grey squares are erased; their adjacent maroon markers stay in place and stamp the nearest edge cell inside the grey square. Pink squares stay pink; their adjacent maroon markers disappear and stamp the corresponding cell on the square's middle row or middle column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:308:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:309:The side touched by a marker determines the projection: grey uses the near edge, while pink uses the centerline, preserving the marker's coordinate along that side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:310:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:311:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/10/prompt.md:312:
